# Git safety

Full workflow: [docs/agents/git-safety.md](../../docs/agents/git-safety.md).

## Branch policy

**Do not create, switch, rename, delete, merge, or rebase branches** unless the user explicitly asked for that exact operation.

Default: work on the **current branch only**. No `git checkout -b`, `git switch -c`, `git branch <name>`, or branch switches "to be safe."

If a branch op seems useful → **stop**, report the exact command, wait for human approval.

## Forbidden (never run without explicit approval)

- `git checkout -b`, `git switch -c`, `git branch <name>`, `git branch -D`
- `git checkout <branch>`, `git switch <branch>`
- `git merge`, `git rebase`, `git reset --hard`, `git worktree add`

## Allowed (typical)

- `git status`, `git diff`, `git log`, `git rev-parse`, `git branch --show-current`
- `git add`, `git commit` — only when user/job explicitly allows
- `git checkout -- <file>` (restore paths, not branches)

## Automation

Runner may create job branches via `prepare_branch`; agents still must not branch-hop mid-job.
